Kept the single delegation but forced the callee to be inlined into this wrapper with GCC's `flatten` attribute, so the hot path becomes one store+return instead of an extra call/jump hop. Semantics are identical since the same setter runs with the same arguments.

```cpp
__attribute__((flatten))
void FieldBase::SetUINT64ZValue(const FIT_UINT64Z value, const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex)
{
    SetUINT64Value(value, fieldArrayIndex);
}
```